body:
Found while reviewing #781 (re-pin to claw `cb83def3`). This predates that PR, and #781 does not make it worse.

The `qc-evidence` job checks no snippet in CI. `references_cache/` is gitignored (`.gitignore:96`, and `git ls-files references_cache` lists only its README), so on a fresh checkout every evidence item is `MISSING_CACHE`. The shared evidence validator exits nonzero only on `SNIPPET_NOT_IN_ABSTRACT`, or on `MISSING_CACHE` under `--strict`, and the workflow does not pass `--strict`.

These CI runs all log `Checked 31 evidence items / MISSING_CACHE 31`:
- 36507224073, #781's head, claw ref `cb83def3`;
- 36504850049, #781's first commit, claw ref `44db08d5`;
- 36396231624, a `main` merge-group run.

`references_cache/README.md` says the abstracts are "committed to the repo so validation runs offline", which the ignore rule contradicts.

Options:
- commit the cache the README describes, and pass `--strict`;
- fetch abstracts in the job;
- rename the job, so it does not read as an evidence check.
